  "question": {
    "text": "Cross-section view of a prism is the equilateral triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> shown in the figure. The minimum deviation is observed using this prism when the angle of incidence is equal to the prism angle. The time taken by light to travel from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> (midpoint of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>) to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is&nbsp;___________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Given, speed of light in vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>)<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e428e013-9369-4ca7-afb8-c3705bf70ea2-image.png\" style=\"width: 223px; height: 212px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>s</mtext></math><br />So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
